{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"disposable-unacademic-millipede","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\n`docs/assets/rebar-demo.svg` uses a deprecated four digit ticket reference, an unconditional bare assignee, stale displayed output, and narration that no longer matches the supported workflow. Ticket weak-amenable-worm records the decision to keep this asset static and text-editable.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Replace deprecated references with supported aliases or two-quad identifiers.\n- Remove the unconditional explicit assignee from the claim example.\n- Align displayed commands, responses, and narration with current CLI contracts.\n- Preserve the static SVG implementation without adding a generator.\n- Preserve the image role, `aria-label`, and README alternative text mechanisms. Update their wording only where the displayed interaction changes.\n- Render and inspect the SVG at normal and narrow display sizes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every displayed ticket reference uses a supported authoring form.\n- [ ] The claim example does not require an explicit assignee.\n- [ ] Displayed output matches current CLI behavior and punctuation.\n- [ ] The narration matches the displayed interaction.\n- [ ] The SVG remains static and text-editable.\n- [ ] The SVG retains its accessibility label and the README retains alternative text.\n- [ ] Rendered normal and narrow views remain legible.","id":"e93d-f75c-1082-4d14","parent_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","accuracy","f16"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"F16 correct the static CLI workflow demonstration"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787509251439893001,"uuid":"1f0657c7-9804-4